  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>The white-spotted pike cichlid, Saxatilia albopunctata, is a pike cichlid from Guyana, Suriname and French Guiana. Its range runs from the Demerara to the Approuague, in slow-moving forest streams, tributaries and pools over sandy substrates, dimly lit by overhanging vegetation. An aggressive species, it can be kept with other large cichlids or on its own, and it grows to about 20 cm, though usually no more than 15 cm in aquaria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Its natural range runs from the Rio Demerara in Guyana, through Suriname to the river Approuague in French Guiana.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Slow moving, forest streams, tributaries and pools, characterised by sandy substrates. Overhanging vegetation creates a dimly-lit atmosphere.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<ul><li>Standard length: 200 mm (20 cm)</li><li>Aquarium base: 120 × 38 cm</li><li>Volume: ~137 litres</li><li>120 × 38 × 30 cm - ~137 litres</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Sand substrate is recommended. This species is likely to dig and arrange the decor to suit itself. Some rockwork should be provided to form caves as pikes like to have an area to which they can retreat. Plants should be robust, ideally potted or rooted to bogwood.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<ul><li>Temperature: 24–27°C</li><li>pH: 6.0–7.0</li><li>Hardness: up to 15 dGH</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Feed a varied diet including a good quality cichlid pellet or flake, live or frozen foods, such as bloodworm or brineshrimp and vegetable matter in the form of spirulina or algae wafers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Aggressive species - may be kept with other large cichlids or as a species only setup.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Male is larger and more colourful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/saxatilia-albopunctata",
      "html": "<p>Limited reports of breeding in the hobby.</p>"
    }
  ],
